ulation:"Modeling and Simulation",Module:"${0} module",Modules:"${0} modules",More:"More",MotorModelingWithSimscape:"Motor Modeling with Simscape Electrical",MotorModelingWithSimscapeIntro:"Learn to create medium and high-fidelity electric motor models in Simscape Electrical and connect them to a controller in Simulink.",MultibodySimulationOnramp:"Multibody Simulation Onramp",MultibodySimulationOnrampIntro:"Learn the basics of modeling and simulating 3D mechanical systems using Simscape Multibody.",MyTemplatesLabel:"My Templates",NewTabTitle:"New",NoSearchQueryResults:'Your search "${0}" did not match any templates.',NoUserTemplates:"You have not created any templates in this group.",OpenExampleLabel:"Open Example",OpenLabel:"Open...",OpenPanelContextClearList:"Clear List",OpenPanelContextRemoveFromList:"Remove from List",OpenPanelHeading:"Open",OpenStatusMessage:'Opening "${0}"',OpenTemplateForEditing:"Opening the template for editing.",PIDControl:"PID Control Techniques",PIDControlIntro:"Design PID controllers for real-world systems.",PowerElectronicsOnramp:"Power Electronics Simulation Onramp",PowerElectronicsOnrampIntro:"Learn the basics of designing and simulating power electronics in Simscape Electrical.",PowerSystemsOnramp:"Power Systems Simulation Onramp",PowerSystemsOnrampIntro:"Learn how to incrementally build and validate power systems using Simscape Electrical.",ProjectConfirmCreateFolderQuestion:"The project folder does not exist. Do you want to create it?",ProjectConfirmCreateFolderTitle:"Create Project Folder",ProjectFromSourcesTitle:"Folder to Project",PurchaseLabel:"You may have access to this content through an online training subscription. To check for access",RecentItemsMenuHeading:"Recent",RecentItemsPlaceHolder:"No Recent Items",RecentModelsHeading:"RECENT MODELS",RecentProjectsHeading:"RECENT PROJECTS",RemoveFavoritesTooltipText:"Remove from favorites",SearchBoxPlaceHolder:"Search",SelectFolderDialogTitle:"Select Folder",SetAsDefaultModelTemplateTooltip:"Use this template for all new models, using Ctrl-N, new_system, or new model buttons",SetAsDefaultSubsystemTemplateTooltip:"Use this template for all new subsystems",SetAsDefaultTemplate:"Set as Default",ShowAllTemplatesLabel:"All",ShowArchitectureTemplatesLabel:"Architecture",ShowLibraryTemplatesLabel:"Library",ShowModelTemplatesLabel:"Model",ShowMoreTemplates:"Show more",ShowProjectTemplatesLabel:"Project",ShowSubsystemTemplatesLabel:"Subsystem",SignIn:"Sign in to take course",SimscapeBatteryOnramp:"Simscape Battery Onramp",SimscapeBatteryOnrampIntro:"Learn the basics of simulating battery systems in Simscape.",SimscapeOnramp:"Simscape Onramp",SimscapeOnrampIntro:"Learn the basics of simulating physical systems in Simscape.",SimulinkFundamentals:"Simulink Fundamentals",SimulinkFundamentalsCourse:"Simulink Fundamentals Course",SimulinkOnramp:"Simulink Onramp",SimulinkOnrampIntro:"Get started quickly with the basics of Simulink.",SimulinkOnrampTooltip:"Interactive introduction to Simulink",SlbeIntro:"Comprehensive training on how to use Simulink, a graphical simulation tool for modeling dynamic physical systems. The course is self-paced and interactive, with hands-on exercises in Simulink.",SlbePrerequisite:"Simulink Onramp or equivalent knowledge of Simulink.",SlbeTitle1:"Simulink Environment Overview",SlbeTitle2:"Modeling Dynamic Systems",SlbeTitle3:"Organizing Growing Models",SlbeTitle4:"Componentizing Models",SlbeTitle5:"Optimizing Simulation Performance",SlbeUnit1:`Learn how to model algorithms in Simulink, visualize and analyze simulation results, and read and write data with Simulink. The Simulink Fundamentals course is divided into five parts. This first part builds on the skills learned in Simulink Onramp course.

This is part of the Simulink Fundamentals course.`,SlbeUnit2:`Model and simulate continuous and discrete dynamic systems in Simulink. Learn how to model differential and difference equations, incorporate transfer function and state-space representations, and simulate physical boundaries and multirate systems.

 This is part of the Simulink Fundamentals course.`,SlbeUnit3:`Create visual and functional hierarchy within a model using Subsystems. Control the execution of subsystems using other signals in your model.

 This is part of the Simulink Fundamentals course.`,SlbeUnit4:`Organize larger projects by referencing other models and creating libraries. Learn how to unit test and accelerate referenced models.

 This is part of the Simulink Fundamentals course.`,SlbeUnit5:`Learn how to improve simulation performance and troubleshoot common performance issues. See how Simulink solves models under various conditions.

